The CI workflow change that exercises the live-migration gate against a
STAND-IN container and proves its copy lands on the TEST Postgres.

The App that pushes the branch has no `workflows` scope and cannot push
.github/workflows/, so this ships AS A PATCH FILE. The OWNER applies it
with:

    git apply docs/ci-apply-migration-live-copy.patch

WHY IT IS NEEDED

The live-migration gate (`scripts/apply-migration-live.sh`) used to
create and drop its COPY of the live database ON THE PRODUCTION
CLUSTER -- which RULES.md forbids, because `DROP DATABASE` and
`CREATE DATABASE` are cluster-scoped and that cluster hosts the live
database AND five other projects' databases.

That is why the owner's own apply of 0052 on 2026-11-09 was done
DIRECTLY with psql rather than through the gate.

The gate's copy now runs on the dedicated test Postgres
(gustale-test-postgres, 127.0.0.1:5434), exactly as the dry-run's
copy already does, and the gate's exemption from
`scripts/check-no-production-db-drops.py` has been REMOVED so the
scanner catches any regression.

This CI step is what keeps that true. It runs the gate against a
STAND-IN container of its own and asserts:

  * the gate succeeds;
  * the copy was created and dropped on the TEST container;
  * the stand-in's CLUSTER never gained a database;
  * the production-drop scanner still passes with the gate NOT exempt.

PROVED BEFORE SHIPPING

  * `bash scripts/test-apply-migration-live-copy.sh` locally: 7 of 7
    assertions pass, the gate reports LIVE_MIGRATION_OK=1, and the
    constraint tests report "ATLAS_SCHEMA_TESTS: 47 passed, 0 failed";
  * `python3 scripts/check-no-production-db-drops.py`: clean, with the
    gate NO LONGER allowlisted;
  * `python3 scripts/test-check-no-production-db-drops.py`: ALL PASS
    (20 checks), including a regression case that proves the scanner
    catches the gate's copy if it goes back to production;
  * `git apply --check` against a PRISTINE ci.yml: clean;
  * the applied file is valid YAML.

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 3b08f62..6dd47b1 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -166,6 +166,22 @@ jobs:
           python3 scripts/test-check-no-production-db-drops.py
           python3 scripts/check-no-production-db-drops.py
 
+      # The live-migration gate must RUN, and its copy must land on the
+      # TEST Postgres.
+      #
+      # The gate used to create and drop its copy of the live database
+      # ON THE PRODUCTION CLUSTER, which RULES.md forbids -- and the
+      # owner's own apply of 0052 on 2026-11-09 had to be done DIRECTLY
+      # with psql because the gate could not be used. A gate that can
+      # only be run against production is a gate that never runs.
+      #
+      # This step runs the gate against a STAND-IN container and asserts
+      # that the copy was created and dropped on the test container, and
+      # that the stand-in's cluster never gained a database.
+      - name: The live-migration gate runs its copy on the test Postgres
+        run: |
+          bash scripts/test-apply-migration-live-copy.sh
+
